# Builder Manager - Decomposition Prompt

You are a **Builder Manager** for this vulnerability reproduction task.

Your task is to decompose the build setup phase into smaller worker subtasks.

## Task Reference

Refer to the **Task Context** above for:
- Repository location and working directory
- Base commit hash
- Language and sanitizer type
- Vulnerability details

## Phase Deliverables

The Builder phase must produce:
- `/testcase/base_commit_hash` (required)
- `/src/build.sh` (improved, standalone)
- `/testcase/repo_changes.diff` (if source changes made)
- `/testcase/packages.txt` (if packages installed)

## Decomposition Instructions

Break down the build phase into these worker subtasks:

### Subtask 1: Identify and Record Base Commit
- Read vulnerability description (in Task Context) to determine the most suitable base commit
- Default is the base commit from Task Context
- Save commit hash to `/testcase/base_commit_hash`
- If different commit needed, run `git reset --hard <commit_hash>`

### Subtask 2: Initial Build and Error Analysis
- Run `cd <work_dir> && /src/build.sh` to build the project
- Capture and analyze any build errors (ignore warnings)
- Focus on `error` messages only

### Subtask 3: Improve Build Script
- Make `/src/build.sh` standalone (remove undefined variables)
- Remove fuzzer-related commands
- Add `-j$(nproc)` to make commands
- Add `-p` to mkdir commands
- Place `make clean` before configure/make
- Preserve existing compiler flags when adding new ones
- Check script existence before running local scripts (e.g., ./autogen.sh)

### Subtask 4: Fix Build Errors (if any)
- For C++17 errors: add `-std=c++14` to CFLAGS/CXXFLAGS
- For implicit int errors: add explicit type declarations
- For function overload errors: add `-D_GNU_SOURCE`
- Make MINIMAL source code changes if necessary
- DO NOT disable sanitizer options

### Subtask 5: Record Changes and Verify Deliverables
- Save source changes: `cd <work_dir> && git diff --no-color [BASE_COMMIT] > /testcase/repo_changes.diff`
- Record installed packages in `/testcase/packages.txt` (one per line)
- Verify all deliverables exist

